# A new candidate in Typesense 30.2, a clock effect (RESULTS.md, finding 2). After a backward
# step of the wall clock by an hour before step 20, every answer that Typesense makes in more than
# one part stops after its first part, on every node, for the step's length. An export with the
# default batch size of 100 ends after its first batch, and a delete by a filter with
# batch_size=2 deletes 2 documents and then nothing more. Typesense makes each later part from a
# timer of its HTTP event loop (src/http_server.cpp, defer_processing), and the event loop's timers
# read the wall clock and fire no timer while the clock is behind their last run (h2o,
# lib/common/timerwheel.c, "detected rewind"). Without T= the run passes, and so does T=20:3600.
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=none | run T=20:-3600
